WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.420
Where did you go this time, Riptoes?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.468
They're cutting right
through that mountain.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.269
Look at the size of
those digging machines.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.000
Long ago, ships sailed all the way around
South America to travel between the

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.647
Atlantic and Pacific Oceans.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.980
The extra 8,000-mile
trip took many months.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.760
Panama is a narrow strip of
land between the two oceans.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.780
A canal is a human-made waterway.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.988
Digging a canal there in Panama
would create a fast shortcut.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
But building it would be
dangerous and difficult.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.701
They almost didn't even
start because of the bugs.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.742
Mosquitoes spread deadly
diseases to the workers.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.520
Finally, an American doctor named William
Gorgas found a way to stop the mosquitoes

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.700
so building could safely begin.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.240
Thousands of workers dug
through the thick jungle.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.260
But a huge mountain blocked the path.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.900
Ships could not sail themselves over it.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.810
But removing the entire
mountain would be too difficult.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.320
So engineers designed a system
of chambers called locks.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.922
They created steps made of water to safely
lift the ships up and over the mountain.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.315
Here's how they work.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.780
A ship sails into a lock and
the gate closes behind it.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.480
Water then fills up or drains out.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.020
The water physically lifts or lowers the
ship until it can enter the next chamber.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.280
This repeats until the
ship is all the way across.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.612
Building the Panama Canal was a huge job.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.150
What kinds of problems do you think
the engineers had to figure out?

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.320
They had to make giant doors strong
enough to hold all the water.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.770
And figure out how to get the water
in the locks to lift the ships.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.660
Engineers had to invent brand new ways to
control water so they could lift ships up

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.300
one side of the mountain and
lower them down the other.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.400
Because of the canal, a trip
that used to take many months now

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.812
takes less than one day.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.040
The Panama Canal opened in 1914.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.820
Today,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:06.230
thousands of ships use it every year to
share food and goods around the world.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.120
What an amazing invention!

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.504
The water does all the lifting.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.350
And it almost didn't happen
because of a bunch of mosquitoes.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.326
I'm glad they figured it out.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.694
Now it only takes a day to
get across instead of months.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.742
If you could build a shortcut to
anywhere, where would you want to go?
